--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Logs_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a72d5d36c70c87c48b8d0b48c416eaf3, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 9634889404416
    m_Localized: "Assistant: Oh wow, I actually made it out alive.\nRecorder: Did
      you find the Professor?\nAssistant: Unfortunately... no.\nAssistant: Looks
      like I was taken to the fish\u2019s lair. It couldn\u2019t digest this hard
      shell, so it spat me out.\nRecorder: That\u2019s incredible... Can you guess
      where you are now?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9953128026112
    m_Localized: "Assistant: Wow, look at those things flying in the sky!\nProfessor:
      Please take a photo for the record.\nAssistant: Got it! I wish I could float
      around in the air like them\u2026\nProfessor: Alright, calm down. Let\u2019s
      assess our current situation: we need to find a way down the cliff.\nRecorder:
      Professor, can you hear me?\nProfessor: Go ahead.\nRecorder: The captain told
      me earlier how to get down. It involves using those... things in the sky.\nRecorder: 
      First, you need to find some yellow fruit nearby, and then\u2026\nProfessor:
      No need to say more\u2014I know what to do. That guy sure has an imagination.\nAssistant:
      The gravity here feels about the same as New Earth. So boring!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775660035969024
    m_Localized: "Captain: Are you all alright?\nProfessor: The logging system is
      intact.\nRecorder: What exactly happened?\nCaptain: \u2026I'm not sure. Could
      you come with me to check the fuel bay?\nRecorder: Alright, Captain"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 779023356071936
    m_Localized: "Recorder: All the fuel leaked out during the crash landing\u2026\nCaptain:
      That\u2019s bad.\nAssistant: Captain, the comms are down too!\nCaptain: Oh
      no\u2026 Let me think.\nProfessor: Stay calm. The rover still works \u2014 
      survey the planet first."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 816514016546816
    m_Localized: "Captain: There's an energy reading near the volcano. I\u2019ll
      head there. You all continue your assigned tasks.\nAssistant: It\u2019s too
      dangerous to go alone!\nProfessor: No objections from me.\nCaptain: We still
      have the recorder to keep us connected. The ship\u2019s failure was my responsibility.
      I\u2019ll find us fuel.\nRecorder: I\u2019ll sync all your collected data to
      the log system. Don\u2019t forget to check your tablets."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 822404048293888
    m_Localized: "Recorder: Captain, the assistant, and the professor have been out
      of contact for five days.\nOnly one week's worth of food left. Whether I find
      fuel or find them\u2026\nI have to go."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1037353529970688
    m_Localized: 'Yellow in appearance

      Has a paralyzing effect on small organisms.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1054716409221120
    m_Localized: Appearance is green, emits a loud noise when struck.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1055946749579264
    m_Localized: "Its shell is hard and can bear a person\u2019s weight.\nIts shell
      shares the same origin as the purple scallop's.\nAfraid of loud sounds."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057724526301184
    m_Localized: 'Normally extends its head antennae above ground as bait.

      After
      swallowing prey, it drags them back into its burrow to eat.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1058771495882752
    m_Localized: 'Afraid of people approaching.

      Can peck open the hard shell
      of the purple scallop.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1061524708331520
    m_Localized: 'Its shell can block strong impacts, but no human force can pry
      it open.

      Eats everything, even what it cannot digest itself.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1068930674790400
    m_Localized: 'Likes eating red fruits.

      Can cross water surfaces.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1070362505318400
    m_Localized: Feeds on ringing fruits, temporarily storing food on its antennae.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1072150130266112
    m_Localized: 'Professor: The ecosystem of this planet is extremely peculiar:
      creatures have no reproductive ability. All new lifeforms are transformed from
      corpses by microorganisms in the soil.

      According to this theory, after
      humans die, they may also become part of this planet in some form.

      I
      was swallowed by a giant creature and severely injured; I may not live for
      long.

      I hope this log is preserved well, so that those who come after
      can see it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1083335059771392
    m_Localized: "Assistant: The last bit of food is gone. Looks like this is where
      it all ends for me, haha.\nAt least I can still stand on high ground to enjoy
      the view at the very end. Not bad.\nThis land feels so warm\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1193298079846400
    m_Localized: "Recorder: Professor, I\u2019ve always wondered why you chose her
      as your assistant. She doesn\u2019t really have any expertise.\nProfessor:
      Her animal-like instincts are perfect for assisting in fieldwork. Back in the
      refugee camp, I noticed her uncanny ability to interpret the weather.\nRecorder:
      She\u2026 was a refugee?\nProfessor: Yes. When I told her I was leaving for
      somewhere even more dangerous, she grew excited and insisted on coming with
      me.\nRecorder: As lively as ever.\nProfessor: She once calmly described to
      me how she witnessed her parents being killed. It seems past suffering left
      no scars on her. Truly a free spirit."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1202927539130368
    m_Localized: "[Day 10] This is a dead volcano\u2026 there\u2019s no energy source
      at all.\nI\u2019m sorry, Professor\u2026 if only I had checked more carefully
      before departure\u2026\n[Day 11] I think I\u2019m stuck here\u2026\n[Day 13]
      Professor, I know you parted ways with me because I was too indecisive. But
      this voyage, I really carried great courage, only to prove it was reckless
      bravery\u2026\nYou\u2019ll probably say again that I wasn\u2019t calm enough,
      haha.\nHonestly, just watching you seriously doing research always made me
      happy. That\u2019s why I agreed to join this journey.\n[Day 16] Maybe ten years,
      fifty years from now, others will come here with better equipment to explore
      this planet.\nAfter all, it looks so fascinating.\nTaking my beloved ship on
      one last flight, dying in the career I love most\u2014there\u2019s nothing
      bad about that."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1845389085446144
    m_Localized: 'Your shooter can store up to five items.


      Press the left
      mouse button to use an item.


      Item order cannot be switched.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1195878386307072
    m_Localized: "Assistant: Your government clerk job is actually pretty stable,
      isn\u2019t it? So why did you join our underfunded ragtag crew?\nRecorder:
      I admire the Professor. When I was reading through the history of the Alliance,
      I came across her name.\nYou may not know this, but as the first person to
      discover a new type of mineral energy, she was once in the spotlight.\nBut
      soon, the news was all about corporations racing to launch ships to the mineral
      planet.\nAnd yet, the Professor quietly continued her deep-space explorations,
      discovering new worlds.\nI think, to her, whether a planet is rich in energy
      or not doesn\u2019t really matter.\nIt\u2019s not hard to see why the Alliance
      eventually stopped funding her\u2014her research interests lay elsewhere.\n\nAssistant:
      When I met her, she was already living so frugally. I never imagined she had
      once been so renowned!\nShe told me she discovered this planet almost at the
      same time as the mineral planet, and she had always wanted to investigate it.\nComing
      here after all these years is like fulfilling a dream for her.\nRecorder: But
      who could have foreseen things would turn out like this\u2026\nAssistant: Haha,
      relax. Scientific exploration always comes with risks\u2014someone has to take
      the first step.\nRecorder: I really envy your optimism\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
